							<td height="50" colspan="3" valign="top" class="windowbg2" align="left"><b>Corona </b> - Pretty much taught me about raids, tactics, strategy, etc - very good and knowledgeable guy. <br /><b>Kiladen </b> - Man, I had to teach this guy how to be a druid back a long time ago when he made his warrior! Then he outleveled me and I owned him in a duel - then I saw the light and switched to a ranger :P.  Good guy, known him since I started EQ.<br /><b>Eretria/Quoits</b> - Hands down two of the best rangers that the server saw early on.  Both helped me learn wtf rangering was about - Eretria put so much into AD/DF that everyone who knew her had to respect her.<br /><b>Tuvas/Demott/Gylen</b> - I still think these 3 are prolly some of the better pallys and better people that I&#039;ve seen play EQ when they were their original characters (I think Demott sold his account).<br /><b>Jeet </b> - One of the best guildleaders I&#039;ve seen.  I only went to EiE because of Corona&#039;s suggestion and his saying that Jeet&#039;s leading style was similar to his own - he was right and I still learned a lot there, even though I could outpull him!<br /><b>Shoog </b> - Shoog was awesome, I&#039;ve been close to em for a long time now and have had fun just BS&#039;ing!<br /><b>Krowbar </b> - What can you say? He was easily the best warrior on the server in the times of AoD/Ascent&#039;s prime and he was in AD/DF for the majority of it.<br /><b>Wixramiablo/Maglan</b> - The funniest shit was when Wix almost beat Mags int he BotB and he was like 4-5 levels lower.  His steal/poof emotes were hilarious too, always caught newbies offguard.<br /><b>Ayrlyn/Tilian </b> - Both these bards knew their class very very well and were very good at what they do.  I would consider them and Baelt to be the top 3 bards on the server til they all quit/left.<br /><br /><br /></td>
